  - Project `{{NAME}}` 0.1.0, C++17. The library `{{NAME_SNAKE}}` is static by default and shared with `-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON`, with the alias `{{NAME_SNAKE}}::{{NAME_SNAKE}}`. The version is compiled in.
  - Warnings (`-Wall -Wextra -pedantic`) are on for gcc and clang and don't fail the build.
  - `{{NAME_SNAKE}}_BUILD_TESTS` is on only when this is the top-level project. With tests on, it uses an installed GoogleTest, or downloads 1.15.2 only if `{{NAME_SNAKE}}_FETCH_GOOGLETEST` is on. With neither, configuring fails and says how to get GoogleTest or turn the tests off. Tests are registered with `gtest_discover_tests`.
  - Install puts the headers, the library and a package with a `SameMajorVersion` version file under `lib/cmake/{{NAME}}`.
- **`template/cmake/{{NAME}}Config.cmake.in`**: the package config file.
