Choices I made, all recorded in the README:
- C++17 is a public requirement, so programs that link the library are compiled as C++17 or later too.
- The static library is built position-independent, so it can also be linked into someone else's shared library.
- Headers are installed by copying the whole `include/` folder, so headers added later are installed too.
